// three.c3 shadow pass, ported to shady for the ShaderDef generator
// (`src/shader/shadow.c3`).
//
// The declarations are gone: the push block comes from the C3 `ShadowPush` the
// pass fills, and the structs it points at come from `abi.c3`'s wire list. What
// is left is the constants and the vertex path - where one vertex of one copy
// lands in the light's clip space.
//
// **This file is the vertex half of both shadow pipelines.** The cut-out variant
// is a second module (`shaders/shadow_cutout.shady`) because shady has no
// preprocessor, and the def hands this same text to both: a pose that drifted
// between the pipeline every caster shares and the one that cuts would be a leaf
// whose shadow is cast from a different place than its neighbours.
//
// What the original says about the shape still holds, and the pose itself is not
// here: it is `shaders/skinning.shady`, which the draw path carries too, so a
// character cannot be lit in one place and shadowed in another.
//
// What remains true of the original:
//
//  - depth is a function of position, so no normal and no colour ride along, and
//    a uv rides along only in the cut-out module;
//  - **a `ShaderMaterial` with a `vertex:` body is not run here**, so such a mesh
//    casts the shadow of its undisplaced geometry. Fixing it means a shadow
//    pipeline per material, which is why it is stated rather than done;
//  - the morph runs before the skin and never after: a blend shape is authored
//    against the rest mesh, and a displacement applied to a vertex the joints
//    have already moved would swing with the limb;
//  - the two skinning paths are here for the same reason the body is: a
//    character's shadow has to be the shadow of the pose it is wearing.

// Where one vertex of one copy lands in the light's clip space.
//
// Split out of the entry points because there are two of them: the depth-only
// one and the cut-out one, which needs a uv beside the position. Both have to
// pose a vertex identically.
fn float4 posed_clip(uint vid, uint iid)
{
	DrawRecord draw = push.draw[0];
	Instance instance = push.instances[iid];

	float3 position = draw.positions[vid];

	// A shadow has to be cast by the face the character is wearing, so the same
	// pose the draw path computes runs here - `shaders/skinning.shady` is that
	// text, used by both. `normal` is a discard: this pass has none, and the
	// shared function writes one.
	float3 unused_normal = float3(0.0, 1.0, 0.0);
	pose_vertex(draw, instance, vid, iid, position, unused_normal);

	// Model first, light second - the same order the main pass uses with the
	// camera, and the only order that makes sense: a joint matrix is in the
	// character's space, the model matrix puts the character in the world, and the
	// light looks at the world.
	return push.projection * (instance.model * float4(position, 1.0));
}
